              "text": "Melbourne’s luxury real estate market—concentrated across the inner-east (Toorak, South Yarra, Armadale, Malvern), the leafy east (Hawthorn, Kew, Canterbury), the Bayside coastline (Brighton), and the Mornington Peninsula (Portsea, Sorrento, Flinders)—is dominated by a small, tightly connected cohort of prestige agencies.\n\nThe premier luxury agencies operating in Melbourne, along with the distinct strengths of each, include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Kay & Burton\n* **Primary Footprint:** Toorak, South Yarra, Bayside, Flinders, Portsea, Sorrento.\n* **Reputation:** The traditional gold standard of Melbourne prestige property.\n* **Why They Are on the Shortlist:** \n  * Kay & Burton has handled many of Melbourne’s grandest estates and architectural landmarks for decades.\n  * They excel at bespoke, editorial-grade marketing campaigns and have established channels into overseas capital (notably across Singapore, Hong Kong, and mainland China).\n  * They have a seamless pipeline connecting Melbourne’s blue-chip enclaves with luxury second homes on the Mornington Peninsula.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Marshall White (Prestige Division)\n* **Primary Footprint:** Stonnington (Toorak, Armadale), Boroondara, and Bayside (Brighton).\n* **Reputation:** The high-volume, record-breaking powerhouse.\n* **Why They Are on the Shortlist:** \n  * Marshall White is one of the most prolific operators in the high-end space, driven by marquee directors like Marcus Chiminello and John Bongiorno.\n  * They frequently set and break Melbourne residential benchmarks, including transacting the historic ~$80 million estate at 29–31 St Georges Road, Toorak.\n  * Their database and cross-office buyer matching across Melbourne’s affluent eastern and southern suburbs are among the deepest in Australia.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Forbes Global Properties / Private Property Global (PPG)\n* **Primary Footprint:** Super-prime Toorak, inner-east estates, and luxury lifestyle properties.\n* **Reputation:** Ultra-prime specialists catering to the top tier of High-Net-Worth Individuals (HNWIs).\n* **Why They Are on the Shortlist:** \n  * Helmed in Melbourne by Michael Gibson and Robert Fletcher (veterans who previously spent decades leading Kay & Burton). \n  * Gibson alone has brokered some of the most expensive sales in Victorian history (such as the former Australian Government House *Stonnington Mansion* for $52 million and repeat sales of multi-tens-of-millions estates along Albany, Irving, and Lansell Roads).\n  * Affiliated with the international Forbes media and luxury real estate syndicate, giving listings direct access to global capital without relying purely on local listing portals.\n\n---\n\n### 4. RT Edgar\n* **Primary Footprint:** Toorak, South Yarra, Boroondara, Bayside, Mornington Peninsula, Bellarine.\n* **Reputation:** Melbourne’s oldest continuous prestige agency (founded in 1896).\n* **Why They Are on the Shortlist:** \n  * Over 130 years of history gives RT Edgar generational relationships with Melbourne’s established old-money families.\n  * Their Toorak office (frequently driven by top performers such as Sarah Case and Jeremy Fox) specializes in significant heritage mansions, subdivisions of landmark estates, and discreet private treaties.\n  * Highly experienced in quiet, high-value off-market negotiations.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Abercromby’s Real Estate\n* **Primary Footprint:** Armadale, Toorak, South Yarra, and Victoria’s country/equestrian estates.\n* **Reputation:** The elite, discreet boutique.\n* **Why They Are on the Shortlist:** \n  * Deliberately avoids the \"high-volume franchise\" model in favor of a boutique, partner-led structure (steered by directors like Jock Langley and Andrew Harlock).\n  * More than 80% of their transactions are referral-based or carried out completely off-market.\n  * If a vendor or buyer prioritizes total privacy away from public inspection queues, auction spectacle, and media scrutiny, Abercromby’s is often their first port of call.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Melbourne Sotheby’s International Realty\n* **Primary Footprint:** Stonnington, Bayside, and the Mornington Peninsula.\n* **Reputation:** The premier international luxury network.\n* **Why They Are on the Shortlist:** \n  * Powered by the global reach of the Sotheby’s brand, this agency is particularly effective for expatriates, international executives, and buyers relocating to Melbourne.\n  * Led by seasoned coastal and metropolitan operators (including Rob Curtain on the Peninsula), their expansion bridges the gap between inner-city luxury penthouses/mansions and Victoria’s finest coastal and winery holdings.\n\n---\n\n### Notable Specialist: Christie's International Real Estate Victoria\n* **Key Agent:** Sean Cussell.\n* **Why Mentioned:** Operates largely as a specialized trophy-home and high-end penthouse dealmaker, having brokered Victorian records across municipalities like Port Phillip (e.g., $30M+ sub-penthouses) and eastern acreage estates.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Recommendation\n* **For Ultra-Prime ($20M–$80M+ trophy estates):** Look toward **Forbes Global Properties (Michael Gibson)**, **Marshall White (Marcus Chiminello)**, or **Kay & Burton**.\n* **For Discretion & Off-Market Selling:** **Abercromby’s** or **RT Edgar**.\n* **For Global & Expatriate Reach:** **Melbourne Sotheby's International Realty** or **Kay & Burton**.",
